saturated|soaked|ADJECTIVE|completely soaked|Completely soaked with liquid.|ướt sũng; thấm đẫm|The cloth was saturated after lying beneath the leaking tap.|Tấm vải ướt sũng sau khi nằm dưới vòi nước bị rò rỉ.|Saturated with a liquid; this everyday wetness sense differs from technical uses involving solutions, fats, or colour.|-
widen|become-broader|VERB|make or become physically broader|To make something physically broader or become broader.|mở rộng; rộng ra|The council widened the pavement beside the school gate.|Hội đồng địa phương mở rộng vỉa hè bên cạnh cổng trường.|Transitive widen something or intransitive something widens; widened is the regular past form.|0
widen|increase-a-range-or-gap|VERB|increase a range or difference|To increase the range of something or make a difference between things greater.|mở rộng; làm gia tăng|The new timetable widened the gap between the two departures.|Lịch chạy mới làm tăng khoảng cách thời gian giữa hai chuyến khởi hành.|Transitive widen a range, choice, or gap; also intransitive a gap widens. The change need not involve physical width.|1
adapt|adjust-yourself|VERB|adjust to changed conditions|To change how you behave or work so that you can manage new conditions.|thích nghi; thích ứng|It took the team a month to adapt to the earlier starting time.|Nhóm mất một tháng để thích nghi với giờ bắt đầu sớm hơn.|Intransitive adapt to something; adapt yourself to something is a related reflexive construction.|0
adapt|convert-a-work|VERB|change a work for a different medium|To change a written or other creative work so that it can be presented in another form.|chuyển thể|The students adapted a short story for a radio performance.|Các sinh viên chuyển thể một truyện ngắn thành một tiết mục phát thanh.|Transitive adapt a work for a medium; adapted from a work identifies the original source.|1
adapt|modify-for-use|VERB|modify for a new use|To change something so that it suits a different use or situation.|điều chỉnh; cải biến cho phù hợp|The carpenter adapted the table to fit the narrow kitchen.|Người thợ mộc cải biến chiếc bàn cho phù hợp với căn bếp hẹp.|Transitive adapt something for a purpose or to do something; distinct from a person adapting to conditions.|2
foundation|building-base|NOUN|base supporting a building|The supporting base on which a building stands.|nền móng; móng nhà|Water collected around the foundation of the abandoned house.|Nước đọng quanh móng của ngôi nhà bỏ hoang.|Countable, often plural foundations for the supporting structure; the foundation of a building identifies what is supported.|0
foundation|basic-support|NOUN|basis for later development|A basic idea, skill, or condition on which something develops.|nền tảng; cơ sở|Regular practice provides a foundation for confident public speaking.|Việc luyện tập đều đặn tạo nền tảng cho khả năng nói trước đám đông một cách tự tin.|Countable; a foundation for something or the foundations of a subject. This is a figurative basis, not a building part.|1
foundation|funding-organisation|NOUN|organisation supporting a cause|An organisation established to support a cause, often by providing money.|quỹ; tổ chức tài trợ|A local foundation paid for the restoration of the community archive.|Một quỹ địa phương chi trả cho việc phục hồi kho tư liệu của cộng đồng.|Countable; a charitable foundation names an organisation. Capitalize it when it forms part of an organisation's proper name.|2
inequality|unequal-treatment-or-opportunity|NOUN|unequal opportunity or treatment|A situation in which people do not have equal opportunities, resources, or treatment.|sự bất bình đẳng|The survey examined inequality in access to public transport.|Cuộc khảo sát xem xét sự bất bình đẳng trong khả năng tiếp cận giao thông công cộng.|Usually uncountable for a general condition; inequalities can name particular differences. Inequality in something identifies the area.|0
